 "summary": "The sign formulas (P = (-1)^(L+1), C = (-1)^(L+S)), the coupling constraints (S \u2264 1, |L\u2212S| \u2264 J \u2264 L+S encoded as L \u2264 J+S \u2227 J \u2264 L+S \u2227 S \u2264 L+J), the closed form (singlet C=-P with P=(-1)^(J+1); triplet C=P except 0^{--}), its negation, and the J \u2264 3 list 0^{--}, 0^{+-}, 1^{-+}, 2^{+-}, 3^{-+} all check out against the standard qqbar analysis, including the degenerate case (L,S,J)=(0,1,0) that the `S \u2264 L + J` conjunct correctly excludes. The predicate has a general witness theorem and consumers, so it is not unexercised, and the module states plainly that the two sign formulas are definitional here with the derivation deferred.",
